comments.body:
@saiarcot895 — good questions:

1. No upstream CI link; the failure is on our internal Chipmunk BMC testbed where the PTF is a standalone `docker run` (no vs/ptf32 topology). CI passes because the KVM topology wires a `mgmt` veth into the PTF, and many CI PTF images still ship classic `ntp`. Both conditions have to be true to hit this.
2. Not a topology change — standalone PTF containers have only had `eth0` all along; the `mgmt` interface is added by the `vs`/KVM topology wiring, not by the PTF image itself. The helper was implicitly relying on that; the probe just makes it work in both cases.
